                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "On this episode of \"going through my library and reviewing games\", we have Chasing the Stars.\n\nI hate to say it, but I really can't recommend this game. The aesthetics, characters, and general idea of it were interesting, but I can't endorse locking a good ending behind a pressured sexual encounter with a certain character. I understand that the devs were trying to make a point about manipulation, but was that really the only way to do it? I tried to unlock all endings and do all routes, but after that, I felt... different about the game. Playing it fatigued me.\n\nOther than that, the story (especially the end) did feel a little rushed and unsatisfying. I could tell what it was going for, but it just didn't quite get there for me. The worldbuilding and characters were interesting enough, but not enough for a replay to get different outcomes.\n\nPlease, for anyone reading this, don't lock good endings behind bad triggers.",
